  "query_preview": "..\nA surge of moisture associated with the northern edge of Invest 99W\nis expected to bring increased showers and isolated thunderstorms for\nGuam and Rota by late tonight or early Saturday and continuing\nthrough Sunday. Rainfall accumulations will likely be highest over\nGuam and decrease to the north with increased distance from 99W.\nHowever, a heavy shower or two cannot be ruled out for Tinian and \nSaipan. If 99W slowly strengthens as expected, then increased trade \nwinds will move in by Sunday for all islands. However, uncertainty \nis high as models struggle to agree on the timing, location, and \nspeed of a tropical disturbance that could form in central Micronesia\nand travel westward, bringing said weather conditions to the region.\nWe will continue to monitor and communicate any updates as necessary.\nModels show a continued wet pattern for Guam and Rota through next \nweek with lower shower chances for islands north of Guam. Another\nsurge of moisture is possible from Invest 90W by the middle of next \nweek but uncertainty remains high for the exact location and strength\nof this system.",
